    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d114-a9">

                <pb facs="0285" n="189" xml:id="pg189"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 7 in No. 61.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Rear-Admiral Patterson to Mr. Holcombe.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Flag-ship Monocacy</hi> (3d rate),<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Yokohama, Japan</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1878-10-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 2, 1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your communication of September 10, in relation to the recent disturbance at
                    Foochow. Previous to its reception I had ordered the United States steamer
                    Alert, Commander R. Boyd, U. S. N., commanding, from Amoy to that place.</p>
                <p>I shall be glad at all times to hear from you in relation to American interests
                    in China, and to co-operate with you in their promotion and protection.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>F. H. PATTERSON,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Rear-Admiral.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
